	"title"		"KF2VR"
	"description"		"[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/optimumbox/Killing-Floor-2-VR/vr-dlss-fixes/docs/workshop/setup-guide.png[/img][h1]How to install for VR (one time, about 2 minutes)[/h1][quote][b]IMPORTANT:[/b] After subscribing, Steam may not download KF2VR until you start the game. Press [b]Play[/b] on Killing Floor 2 once, wait for the main menu, then quit. If the 3817663661 folder below is missing or empty, do that again and wait a minute.[/quote][olist][*]Click [b]Subscribe[/b]. Then press [b]Play[/b] on Killing Floor 2 once, wait for the main menu, and quit the game.[*]In your Steam Library, right-click [b]Killing Floor 2[/b] > [b]Manage[/b] > [b]Browse local files[/b]. A folder called killingfloor2 opens.[*]In that window's address bar, click [b]steamapps[/b]. Then open these folders, one after another: [b]workshop[/b] > [b]content[/b] > [b]232090[/b] > [b]3817663661[/b].[*]Double-click [b]Setup KF2VR[/b] in that folder. Click [b]OK[/b]: Steam closes and opens again by itself.[*]Press [b]Play[/b] on Killing Floor 2 and choose [b]Play in VR[/b] or [b]Play normally[/b].[/olist]To remove it, double-click [b]Setup KF2VR[/b] again. Your normal Killing Floor 2 is never changed: Play normally starts the plain game.[h2]Prefer not to run the setup file? Do it by hand instead[/h2]It does exactly the same thing.[olist][*]Do steps 1 to 3 above.[*]Right-click the file [b]Play.cmd[/b] (it may show just as [b]Play[/b]) and choose [b]Copy as path[/b]. On Windows 10, hold [b]Shift[/b] while right-clicking to see that option.[*]In Steam, right-click [b]Killing Floor 2[/b] > [b]Properties[/b]. On the [b]General[/b] page, click in the [b]Launch Options[/b] box and press [b]Ctrl+V[/b] to paste.[*]After what you pasted, type one space, then type: [b]%command%[/b][*]Close the Properties window and press [b]Play[/b] on Killing Floor 2.[/olist]Check the box: it starts with a quote mark and your drive letter, ends with Play.cmd and a quote mark, then a space and %command%. Copy as path adds the quote marks for you. To remove it later, empty the Launch Options box.[h1]No VR headset? Play on your normal screen with VR friends[/h1]You do NOT need a headset to join friends who play in VR. Pick ONE of these two ways:[h2]Way 1: Server browser (easiest)[/h2][olist][*]Subscribe to this item (you don't need the one-time install above for this way).[*]Press [b]Play[/b] on Killing Floor 2. If a window asks how you want to play, click [b]Play normally[/b].[*]In the game's main menu, open the [b]Server Browser[/b].[*]Search for your friend's server by its name (ask your friend what they called it), click it, and join.[*]Type the server password your friend gives you.[/olist][h2]Way 2: Join code[/h2][olist][*]Do the one-time VR install at the top of this page (it is needed for the launcher).[*]Press [b]Play[/b] on Killing Floor 2 and click [b]Play in VR (KF2-VR)[/b]. Don't worry: this opens the KF2-VR launcher, which also works without a headset.[*]In the launcher, choose [b]Desktop - no headset[/b].[*]Click [b]Join a friend[/b]. Ask your friend for their join code (a long line starting with KF2VR1:), copy it, click [b]Paste code[/b], then click [b]Join[/b].[/olist]The game, your friend's server and your KF2-VR files must all be the same version. If joining fails, check that Steam has finished updating the Workshop items, then try again.[h1]About[/h1]The unofficial Killing Floor 2 VR mod by Kvasir94 and optimumbox for PC VR headsets (Windows, Steam copy of Killing Floor 2). Updates arrive through Steam automatically. VR sessions run with VAC off: never use the VR mod on VAC-secured servers. Fan-made, not affiliated with Tripwire Interactive. Source and releases: https://github.com/optimumbox/Killing-Floor-2-VR"
	"changenote"		"__CHANGENOTE__"
}
